      "source": [
        "## 6. Train/Test Split and SMOTE"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "4dc2360f"
      },
      "source": [
        "We will split the data into training and testing sets to evaluate our models on unseen data. Due to the highly imbalanced nature of fraud detection datasets, we will apply Synthetic Minority Over-sampling Technique (SMOTE) to the training set only, to balance the classes and help our models learn better from the minority (fraudulent) class."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "787c5b35",
        "outputId": "34e8aa5e-9465-465a-e4bb-35152a82b465"
      },
      "source": [
        "# Split the data into training and testing sets\n",
        "X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(X, y, test_size=0.3, random_state=42, stratify=y)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"Original training set shape: X_train {X_train.shape}, y_train {y_train.shape}\")\n",
        "print(f\"Original testing set shape: X_test {X_test.shape}, y_test {y_test.shape}\")\n",
        "print(f\"Original training set fraud distribution:\\n{y_train.value_counts(normalize=True)}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Apply SMOTE to the training data only\n",
        "sm = SMOTE(random_state=42)\n",
        "X_train_res, y_train_res = sm.fit_resample(X_train, y_train)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"\\nResampled training set shape: X_train_res {X_train_res.shape}, y_train_res {y_train_res.shape}\")\n",
        "print(f\"Resampled training set fraud distribution:\\n{y_train_res.value_counts(normalize=True)}\")"
      ],
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
